## Bugs
1. **Duplicated words in agent replies.** After a service restart, opening a chat triggered two simultaneous `session/load` RPCs for the same session (`resume-session` action + `loadSavedChatSessionForSend` in the send path). Both checked `knownSessions` before either finished, so the CLI subscribed twice and every `session/update` chunk was emitted twice for the life of the agent process.
2. **Filter shows miscagent while the open chat belongs to agent.dev.** The filter is per-browser (localStorage) while `lastChatId` is per-user (server, shared across devices). Initial restore opened the last chat without reconciling the filter.

## Fix
- `lib/acp/runtimeState.ts`: new `loadSessionOnce` shares an in-flight `session/load` promise per session; used by all three call sites in `app/api/acp/route.ts`. Failures reject all waiters and allow retry.
- `useChatRuntime.ts`: on initial restore, if the restored chat has an `agentId` different from the active filter, the filter switches to that agent. Chats without agentId keep existing behavior.

## Tests
- New `tests/acp-session-load-once.test.ts` (concurrent dedupe, failure + retry).
- New Playwright test: restoring an alpha chat with filter persisted as beta switches the filter to alpha. All 9 tests in `test-filter-scroll-history.spec.ts` pass locally.
- `tsc` clean; route source assertions updated.

No new UI surface; the filter dropdown simply shows the correct agent.
